# gate-matrix golden — RECORDS CURRENT BEHAVIOUR, NOT DESIRED BEHAVIOUR.
#
# Several rows deliberately freeze KNOWN DEFECTS so that fixing them shows up
# as an intended diff rather than passing unnoticed. Each is listed with the
# delta a correct fix SHOULD produce, so a reviewer can tell an expected
# change from a regression without re-deriving it:
#
#   gate11-open-questions   now: state=N and an EMPTY systemMessage — a
#                           genuine question deletes the state silently, so
#                           the user cannot resume after answering it.
#                           after Release A: decision=approve, state=N
#                           (UNCHANGED), marker removed, and a NON-EMPTY
#                           systemMessage naming the brief and the bullet.
#                           Terminal cleanup is deliberately KEPT in A;
#                           resumability needs the Release C resume path
#                           and is out of scope until then. Do not expect
#                           state=Y here or a correct A reads as partial.
#   gate11n1-none-bullet    now: STOPS on a '- 없음' placeholder — the
#                           false positive measured at 77% of briefs
#                           after a fix: decision=block (advances)
#   gate11n2-h3-heading     now: decision=block — ADVANCES past a real
#                           question under a '###' heading (the regex demands
#                           exactly '## ').
#                           after a fix: identical to gate11-open-questions,
#                           i.e. approve / state=N / non-empty systemMessage.
#   gate11n3-star-bullet    now: decision=block — ADVANCES past a real
#                           question on a '*' bullet, though '*' IS a list
#                           marker elsewhere in the same file.
#                           after a fix: same as gate11n2 above.
#   gate01-bad-json         now: state=N — a merely CORRUPT file (killed
#                           editor save, disk-full) is deleted, discarding
#                           a recoverable iteration count and baseline SHA
#   gate03-inactive         now: fine. Becomes a defect if a pause ever
#                           sets active=false — this row is then the
#                           silent-deletion path on the next fire.
#   gate10b-max-minutes     now: state=N — the wall-clock cap deletes
#                           state rather than pausing it
#   gate10-max-iterations   now: state=N — same class as gate10b. If a fix
#                           converts cap-termination to a pause, expect TWO
#                           diffs here, not one.
#   gate06-idle-timeout     now: state=N and an EMPTY systemMessage — 24h of
#                           idleness deletes the loop silently. This is the
#                           exact hazard midflight M5 guards against, frozen
#                           here as if acceptable.
#   gate08-plan-relative    now: state=N — a recoverable CONFIGURATION error
#                           destroys state, same class as gate01. (A plan
#                           path that is absolute but missing takes the same
#                           fail_open branch and has no row at all.)
#   gate06b-stale-crosssession  now: state=Y — a state that is BOTH long
#                           past the idle timeout AND owned by a session that
#                           no longer exists is PRESERVED, because Gate 4
#                           pauses on session mismatch and the idle GC sits
#                           behind it. The dead state never gets collected and
#                           every later fire pauses again — 214 fires / 58% of
#                           the field baseline.
#                           after a fix: state=N, log = idle timeout
#   gate06c-stale-marker-fresh-lease  now: state=N — an in-flight marker
#                           gives no protection at all, so a loop that was
#                           mid-iteration is collected rather than handed to
#                           Gate 7.
#                           after a fix: state=Y (exempt while the lease holds)
#   gate06d-stale-marker-expired-lease  now AND after a fix: state=N.
#                           Deliberately unchanged. It is the other side of
#                           6c: once the lease expires the marker stops
#                           excusing the state. If 6c and 6d ever agree, the
#                           exemption has stopped being bounded and defect B
#                           is back in a new form.
#   gate09b-dirty-blocks    PARTLY FIXED (B-3) — the pause now carries a
#                           systemMessage naming the gitignore patterns, so
#                           it is no longer silent. Completion is still
#                           unreachable while an untracked state file or
#                           brief keeps the tree dirty: that is the correct
#                           refusal, and the guidance in commands/ + README
#                           is what stops a compliant repo from hitting it.
#   gate09c-plan-outside-repo  FIXED (B-3) — no longer a frozen defect.
#                           It used to declare 'all tasks complete' and
#                           delete state over a DIRTY repo, because Gate 9
#                           checked dirname(plan_path) instead of REPO_ROOT
#                           and a plan at the /plan default is outside any
#                           repo, skipping the check entirely. Now pins the
#                           repaired behaviour: SOFT-PAUSE, state=Y
#                           active=true. Reverting to state=N here means
#                           the repo-scope fix regressed.
#   gate04-session-mismatch now: active=true after a CROSS-SESSION pause and
#                           an EMPTY systemMessage, so the state stays armed
#                           and the user sees a turn end with no explanation.
#                           This is the field baseline's single most frequent
#                           event (214 fires / 58%).
#                           after a fix: active=false, non-empty message.
#   gate05-no-continuation  now: same shape as gate04, but this is a
#                           SAME-session pause — the user may well intend to
#                           resume. Do NOT fold it in with gate04: disarming
#                           it would kill a loop its owner still wants.
#                           after a fix: message only; active stays true.
#   gate12-lock-held        FIXED (B-2b) — no longer a frozen defect. It now
#                           pins the repaired behaviour: lock=Y, because a
#                           non-owner must not rmdir, plus a systemMessage
#                           telling the user how to clear a stale lock (the
#                           deleted rmdir was also the only stale-lock
#                           cleanup). If this row returns to lock=N,
#                           ownership tracking has regressed.
#                           NOTE, measured: simply deleting the rmdir from
#                           soft_pause() flips SIX rows — gate02, gate04,
#                           gate05, gate05b, gate09b, gate12 — because five
#                           of them legitimately acquire the lock and would
#                           then leak it. Those five reading lock=N is what
#                           proves owner paths still release rather than leak.
#
# Do not read this file as a specification. A diff here is a question
# ("did I mean to change this?"), not automatically a failure. Regenerating
# with --update is how you ACCEPT a delta — walk the rows above first.
#
# Columns (6, pipe-separated):
#   1 label  2 decision  3 state/active/marker(value)/lock/iter
#   4 reason fingerprint (sentinel line + enforcement-clause count)
#   5 systemMessage  6 log tail
# Regenerate: bash tests/gate-matrix.test.sh --update
advance-inject             | block   | state=Y active=true  marker=Y(2) lock=N iter=2/2 | sentinel="[dual-review-loop iter 2/20]" enforce=1 | dual-review-loop plan iter 2/20 | iter 2 → injecting (brief target: <TMP>/.claude/reviews/iter-002.md)
gate00-no-state            | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | 
gate01-bad-json            | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | FAIL-OPEN: state file is not valid JSON
gate02-schema-unknown      | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=N iter=1/0 | - | dual-review-loop paused: state schema 'v9' unknown. To resume: install a hook supporting this schema, OR run /dual-review-loop:cancel-loop (or rm <TMP>/.claude/dual-review-loop.state.json) to start over. | SOFT-PAUSE: schema mismatch (got=v9 expected one of: v1 v2) — state preserved; downgrade hook or cancel manually (state preserved)
gate03-inactive            | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | state.active != true
gate04-session-mismatch    | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=N iter=1/0 | - |  | SOFT-PAUSE: different session (test-session != other-session) (state preserved)
gate05-no-continuation     | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=N iter=1/1 | - |  | SOFT-PAUSE: no continuation signal (last_injected_iter=1, gap=<N>s) — user likely took control (state preserved)
gate05a-grace-inside       | block   | state=Y active=true  marker=Y(2) lock=N iter=2/2 | sentinel="[dual-review-loop iter 2/20]" enforce=1 | dual-review-loop plan iter 2/20 | iter 2 → injecting (brief target: <TMP>/.claude/reviews/iter-002.md)
gate05b-grace-outside      | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=N iter=1/1 | - |  | SOFT-PAUSE: no continuation signal (last_injected_iter=1, gap=<N>s) — user likely took control (state preserved)
gate06-idle-timeout        | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | idle timeout (>86400s)
gate06b-stale-crosssession | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=N iter=1/0 | - |  | SOFT-PAUSE: different session (test-session != vanished-session) (state preserved)
gate06c-stale-marker-fresh-lease | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | idle timeout (>86400s)
gate06d-stale-marker-expired-lease | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | idle timeout (>86400s)
gate07-inflight-nocommit   | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=Y(1) lock=N iter=1/0 | - | dual-review-loop: iter 1 has not committed yet (plan mode can block commits, or it stopped early). It auto-resumes the moment a commit lands — exit plan mode and let it finish. If this iteration legitimately produced no commit, run /dual-review-loop:cancel-loop (or rm .claude/dual-review-loop.inflight). | in-flight marker present (iter=1) — no commit detected; not advancing (base_sha=<SHA>)
gate08-plan-relative       | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | FAIL-OPEN: plan_path not absolute: relative/plan.md
gate09a-all-complete       | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | all tasks complete after 1 iterations
gate09b-dirty-blocks       | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=N iter=1/0 | - | dual-review-loop: every task in the plan is complete, but the working tree still has uncommitted changes, so the loop did not declare completion. Commit or stash them and the loop finishes on the next turn. If the changes are plugin artifacts, add .claude/dual-review-loop.*, .claude/dual-review-loop/ and .claude/reviews/ to .gitignore. | SOFT-PAUSE: no unfinished tasks but uncommitted changes present (state preserved)
gate09c-plan-outside-repo  | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=N iter=1/0 | - | dual-review-loop: every task in the plan is complete, but the working tree still has uncommitted changes, so the loop did not declare completion. Commit or stash them and the loop finishes on the next turn. If the changes are plugin artifacts, add .claude/dual-review-loop.*, .claude/dual-review-loop/ and .claude/reviews/ to .gitignore. | SOFT-PAUSE: no unfinished tasks but uncommitted changes present (state preserved)
gate10-max-iterations      | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | max_iterations reached (20 >= 20)
gate10b-max-minutes        | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | max_minutes reached (<N>s >= 60s / 1min cap)
gate11-open-questions      | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | Open Questions detected in last brief — user decision needed
gate11n1-none-bullet       | approve | state=N active=-     marker=N(-) lock=N iter=-/- | - |  | Open Questions detected in last brief — user decision needed
gate11n2-h3-heading        | block   | state=Y active=true  marker=Y(2) lock=N iter=2/2 | sentinel="[dual-review-loop iter 2/20]" enforce=1 | dual-review-loop plan iter 2/20 | iter 2 → injecting (brief target: <TMP>/.claude/reviews/iter-002.md)
gate11n3-star-bullet       | block   | state=Y active=true  marker=Y(2) lock=N iter=2/2 | sentinel="[dual-review-loop iter 2/20]" enforce=1 | dual-review-loop plan iter 2/20 | iter 2 → injecting (brief target: <TMP>/.claude/reviews/iter-002.md)
gate12-lock-held           | approve | state=Y active=true  marker=N(-) lock=Y iter=1/0 | - | dual-review-loop: another hook instance holds the lock, so this turn did not advance. If no other loop is running, the lock is stale — remove it with: rmdir .claude/dual-review-loop.lock | SOFT-PAUSE: lock contention (state preserved)
